# xLaDe Metrics

Metrics are used to measure the performance in xLaDe.
They can be used to measure CLI, experiments, scripts, performance etc.
Metrics should be quantitative, measurable, and comparable.

---

## Examples:

- Benchmarking xLaDe 
- Total time to get output of experiment
- CLI overhead
- Installation time
- Tools, scripts, etc. timings
- Resource usage
- RAM, CPU, and other resource usage
- Comparison between xLaDe and other tools

and so on.

---

## Non-metrics

- Benchmarking Lean 4

//--
Jailbreak idea - Create an experiment with Lean 4
Then benchmark Lean 4 as an experiment
--//

---

## Purpose

- Helping make xLaDe better
- Reducing friction
- Evaluating xLaDe performance 

---

## Current Status

We haven't developed metrics yet.
But it would be eventually developed.
We request community to come up with some ideas and help in its development.

